//! The interactive inbox in a native window: platform/window for the window and input,
//! ui-tree-window to turn window events into tree input, the tree for hover, press, focus,
//! tab order and nested scrolling, and ui_renderer on WebGPU (Dawn) for the frame.
//!
//!   ui-tree-demo [--check] [--editor]
//!
//! `--editor` shows the editor fixture instead: text fields to type into, with the platform's
//! input method (try a Japanese one), the clipboard, undo and pointer selection.
//!
//! The demo is also a tiny client: it reads the tree's event records and answers clicks with
//! mutations. New appends a row and scrolls it into view; Archive removes the focused row.
//! Tab and Shift+Tab move focus, Enter and Space press the focused button, the wheel and the
//! scrollbar thumbs scroll the list and the box nested in it.
//!
//! In a debug build with `SILK_UI_INSPECT` set, the demo also serves the inspector protocol, so
//! `ui-inspect-cli` (ui/inspect/cli) can snapshot it, click its buttons and take screenshots;
//! `scripts/demo inspect` runs that under Xvfb.
//!
//! `--check` ignores real input. It draws a frame, feeds a scripted hover, wheel and Tab to the
//! tree, draws two more, checks the tree's state, reads the window's surface back and compares
//! it with the CPU reference of the same frame. Exit code 0 within tolerance, 1 outside, 2 on
//! an error.
import ui_fixtures.fixtures as fixtures
import ui_tree.lib {
  UiTree,
  TreeError,
  Batch,
  FrameInput,
  CpuSnapshot,
  Event as Record,
  EventKind,
  Input,
  NodeKind,
  Mutation,
  NONE
}
